1
00:00:00,393 --> 00:00:03,443
Eighty-six to ninety-three
million dollars, stolen.

2
00:00:03,817 --> 00:00:05,445
From over three hundred wallets.

3
00:00:05,805 --> 00:00:08,068
One reseller. Seven markets halted.

4
00:00:08,403 --> 00:00:10,502
Genuine Check? Still passes.

5
00:00:10,552 --> 00:00:12,229
The implant is an extra board.

6
00:00:12,561 --> 00:00:13,933
And extra boards have weight.

7
00:00:15,083 --> 00:00:16,348
This is tamper-check.

8
00:00:16,398 --> 00:00:18,174
Weight is the primary signal:

9
00:00:18,224 --> 00:00:20,195
three or more readings
on a milligram scale,

10
00:00:20,245 --> 00:00:23,013
averaged, against a reference
from the same batch.

11
00:00:23,063 --> 00:00:24,720
Reference weights here are examples.

12
00:00:24,770 --> 00:00:29,650
This unit is plus seven milligrams.
Risk zero. Likely genuine.

13
00:00:30,743 --> 00:00:32,290
Now, glue on one side.

14
00:00:32,340 --> 00:00:34,361
Plus three hundred fifty-nine milligrams.

15
00:00:34,411 --> 00:00:37,745
In 3D, green is the
expected center of mass,

16
00:00:37,795 --> 00:00:42,219
yellow the estimate, red the
suspected added mass. Suspicious.

17
00:00:43,307 --> 00:00:44,749
A simulated cellular implant.

18
00:00:44,799 --> 00:00:48,101
Powered off in a Faraday bag,
a Ledger should be silent.

19
00:00:48,151 --> 00:00:49,704
It has no cellular radio.

20
00:00:49,754 --> 00:00:54,894
Here, bursts every thirty
seconds, plus 1.2 grams. Tampered.

21
00:00:54,944 --> 00:00:56,219
Risk one hundred.

22
00:00:57,311 --> 00:01:00,907
On a one-gram kitchen scale, three
hundred milligrams simply vanish.

23
00:01:00,957 --> 00:01:03,267
The tool flags it: demo only.

24
00:01:04,355 --> 00:01:06,593
At a thousandth of a gram, it's caught:

25
00:01:06,643 --> 00:01:10,023
plus three hundred twelve
milligrams. Then the checklist.

26
00:01:10,073 --> 00:01:13,769
Don't enter a seed. Genuine
Check can't see added boards.

27
00:01:13,819 --> 00:01:17,741
Move funds to a new device bought
directly from Ledger, with a new seed.

28
00:01:18,940 --> 00:01:21,251
Weight tells you that mass was added.

29
00:01:21,301 --> 00:01:22,910
Two scales tell you where.

30
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:27,888
Step one: lay a rigid ruler across two
milligram scales, a hundred millimeters

31
00:01:27,938 --> 00:01:30,823
apart. Step two:
tare both, with the ruler on.

32
00:01:30,873 --> 00:01:34,141
Step three: lay the wallet in the
middle. Step four:

33
00:01:34,191 --> 00:01:35,417
read left and right.

34
00:01:35,467 --> 00:01:37,970
Equal readings mean the mass is centred.

35
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:42,860
The offset is right minus left, over the
total, times half the span.

36
00:01:42,910 --> 00:01:44,796
But you never place it perfectly.

37
00:01:44,846 --> 00:01:49,021
So rotate the wallet a hundred eighty
degrees, in place, and read again.

38
00:01:49,071 --> 00:01:50,840
The wallet's offset flips sign.

39
00:01:50,890 --> 00:01:52,541
Your placement error doesn't.

40
00:01:52,591 --> 00:01:56,942
Half the difference keeps the real
offset, and cancels the placement error.

41
00:01:57,890 --> 00:02:02,279
In the tool, open section three:
Two scales. The numbers here are

42
00:02:02,329 --> 00:02:03,576
simulated examples.

43
00:02:04,530 --> 00:02:05,922
Here's a genuine unit.

44
00:02:05,972 --> 00:02:10,840
Left and right, then the flipped pair,
and the span: a hundred millimeters.

45
00:02:11,790 --> 00:02:14,000
The tool computes x one and x two.

46
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:18,652
About one millimeter of placement error
is cancelled. The real offset:

47
00:02:18,702 --> 00:02:21,244
minus zero point two eight millimeters.

48
00:02:22,190 --> 00:02:25,659
The example tolerance is zero point
seven millimeters.

49
00:02:25,709 --> 00:02:28,266
Inside it, the center of mass is normal.

50
00:02:28,316 --> 00:02:29,244
Likely genuine.

51
00:02:30,190 --> 00:02:31,442
Now the implant unit.

52
00:02:31,492 --> 00:02:36,092
The offset is plus zero point eight five
millimeters, toward the right end.

53
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:40,652
That's past the tolerance, so the center
of mass is flagged.

54
00:02:40,702 --> 00:02:45,230
Past twice the tolerance, it would be
high. With one point two extra grams,

55
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:46,878
and radio bursts:
tampered.

56
00:02:47,830 --> 00:02:51,384
In the 3D view, green is the expected
center of mass.

57
00:02:51,434 --> 00:02:56,824
Yellow is the measured one, exaggerated
five times. Red marks the end where mass

58
00:02:56,874 --> 00:02:57,980
was likely added.

59
00:02:58,930 --> 00:03:03,770
Until a wallet is verified, keep it in a
Faraday bag, so an implant can't reach

60
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:07,360
the network. Test the bag:
put a phone inside and call it.

61
00:03:07,410 --> 00:03:09,464
If it rings, the bag doesn't work.

62
00:03:10,599 --> 00:03:11,821
Weigh before you trust.
